5.18  2026-09-01

    - TKT-690. replace_records listed comments and checklist among its
      mutable fields, and _replace_value recursed into every array and
      hash it met, rewriting every scalar leaf - not only the prose those
      two structures hold, but also identity (id), status, timestamps and
      a checklist item's recorded proof. Measured: 'done' -> 'FINISHED'
      on --field checklist silently turned a completed item into one
      every gate reads as unfinished; '0' -> '9' turned CHK-001 into
      CHK-991 and a valid date into an impossible one (month 98).

      comments and checklist are now restricted to their one genuine
      prose leaf - the comment body, and a checklist item's text -
      declared in a named allow-list rather than inferred from shape.
      Every other leaf (id, author, status, timestamps, recorded proof)
      is left alone, and a pattern that would have matched one of them is
