      poll being added there.

      Fixed by adding both routes to %POLLED. hero-counts.js's own
      60-second /tasklist poll (TKT-797) is covered by the same fix,
      since the exemption is per-route. New test t/474.
      docs/commands.md updated.

5.13  2026-09-01

    - TKT-806. tasklist_add had zero deduplication - a brand-new item on
      every call, even when a pending or working item already existed for
      the same --ref and session. Hit three separate times in one real
      session (TKT-675, TKT-788, TKT-793): each card already had a
      pickup item from an earlier session, and a fresh one went
      unnoticed until a manual cross-check of the shared list.

      Fixed as a soft signal, not a hard refusal, matching tasklist's own
      sticky-note design (Q-075): the new item carries a
      possible_duplicate key naming the existing item's id and text, but
      is created regardless - a caller may genuinely want two distinct
      tasks on one card. A done item does not count as still owed, an
      unrelated card's item is never compared, and an item with no --ref
      at all has nothing to compare against. New test t/473.
      docs/commands.md updated.

