4.89  2026-08-30

    - TKT-652. Renaming a column's entry-required-action wording
      silently un-gated every card already carrying an item under the
      old text.

      The entry gate (_column_entry_required_action_violation) matched
      a required_items entry against the column's live entry template
      by TEXT alone. That is right as far as it goes - TKT-445/t/422
      established that a manual required-action.add item satisfies a
      column's own template exactly like a template-derived one, "do
      the work early" is a real, intentional capability. What text
      matching alone got wrong: change the template's wording and
      every card already carrying an item under the OLD wording stops
      matching and silently stops gating, with no signal that anything
      changed.

      Fixed by adding an `entry` marker, stamped on any item genuinely
      populated from a column's entry template. The gate now trusts
      the marker OR a live text match - either is sufficient - so a
      rename cannot un-gate a marked item, and doing the work early
      still gates entry the same way it has always gated exit.

      A first version of this fix required the marker EXCLUSIVELY,
      dropping the text-match path entirely on the theory that a
      manual item satisfying an entry requirement was itself the bug.
      It was not: t/422 (TKT-657, TKT-445) went red under it - a
      manually-added, already-Done item stopped being recognized as
      "already there", and a fresh duplicate pending item was created
      and announced as outstanding on the very next move, even though
      the work was already proven. Caught only after this card had
      already reached pending-push and the coverage/suite re-run
      surfaced the regression; corrected before commit by restoring
      the plain text+column dedup in required_item_add,
      _populate_entry_required_actions, and
      _populate_column_required_actions, and changing the entry
      gate's own check from `entry` alone to `entry || live text
      match`.

      New test t/449-a-required-item-with-no-memory-of-where-it-came-
      from.t: doing the entry work early still gates entry (symmetric
      with exit), a genuine entry item still gates normally, a renamed
      entry template does not un-gate an item already marked under the
      old wording, and an exit-template item carries the template
      marker but never the entry one.

      Also closes a coverage gap left by the already-shipped TKT-632
      (4.86): _reset_linked_tasks_on_return's genuine-tasklist-failure
      branch had no test exercising it, found while verifying this
      card (lib/Tira/CLI.pm sat at 99.5%, not 100%). New assertion in
      t/446-a-move-that-cancels-its-own-side-effect.t corrupts the
      tasklist storage file directly and confirms the failure is
      reported rather than swallowed.

