    - TKT-704. The documented count of police rules is held to what the engine
      reports, in every document and every phrasing. It was stated three times
      and checked once: README and SKILLS both said "40 rules police", SKILLS
      also said "the 36 rules police itself" two thousand lines earlier, and the
      guard matched "(\d+) rules cover" - one sentence of the three. So every
      rule added since demanded that one sentence be updated and said nothing
      about the other two, and the stale one sat four rules behind. The guard's
      existence is what made it invisible: a number nobody checks is obviously
      unreliable and gets re-read; a number that is checked reads as reliable.
      t/433 walks every markdown file the repository carries outside its build
      and dependency directories, and matches the shape of a claim - a number
      ahead of the word "rules", with at most two words between them - rather
      than a wording somebody thought of, so a third phrasing in a document nobody
      listed is caught too. Review widened that shape once before it shipped:
      it began as "<number> rules <verb>", which heard "40 rules cover" and
      "40 rules police" but not "40 police rules" or "40 policy rules", and the
      wider shape was measured across all 121 documents first - same three
      claims, no false positives. Two evasions came out of the same review and
      are controls in the fixture now: a claim indented under a bullet is a
      paragraph continuation rather than an example, and a fence indented four
      spaces is not a fence, which is the SKILLS.md failure below reproduced
      inside the tool that detects it. A number inside
      a fenced or indented example is left alone: a transcript records what was
      true when it was taken, and demanding history be rewritten on every rule
      added is how a guard earns being ignored. The narrow check in
      t/03-metadata.t is retired rather than kept beside it, because two checks
      of one fact is the shape that produced the bug.

