4.16  2026-08-26

    - TKT-538. Every tasklist mutation command (update, remove,
      task.attach.add/discard, task.ref.link/unlink) now refuses to act
      on an item belonging to a different --session than the caller's,
      with the same "No task" error an unknown id gets. _tasklist_find_item
      previously looked an item up by id alone - since TSK ids are
      sequential and project-wide, a completely different session could
      silently edit or permanently delete another session's private
      item just by guessing its id, defeating the isolation --session
      exists for (TKT-505) far more seriously than TKT-537's read-only
      version of the same gap. Self-found and reproduced directly while
      fixing TKT-537. Also fixed a related pre-existing CLI bug found
      along the way: the reminder-settings guard's tasklist exemption
      regex never matched the 4 nested tasklist.task.attach/ref
      sub-verbs (dotted four deep, not two), so --session was rejected
      outright on exactly the commands this fix needed it most on.

