4.04  2026-08-25

    - TKT-526. Fixed a genuine flake in t/373-a-singleton-that-kills-its-
      rival.t under parallel test runs (prove -j). Its real-fork subtest
      sent SIGTERM to a freshly-forked child racing that child's own
      $SIG{TERM} = ... assignment; under heavy CPU contention (several
      concurrent prove/Devel::Cover processes) that window widened enough
      for the signal to be lost outright, and the child ran its full
      30-second sleep to completion instead of exiting cleanly. Reproduced
      directly: 8-way parallel runs of the file alone failed on exactly
      this assertion, the failing run taking the full 30 wallclock
      seconds. Fixed with a pipe-based readiness handshake - the child
      closes its write end right after installing the handler, and the
      parent blocks reading before sending anything - closing the race
      rather than papering over it with a longer sleep. Verified with
      24/24 concurrent solo runs of the file and 5/5 full-suite -j8 runs,
      all clean.

4.03  2026-08-25

    - TKT-524. Task List cards accept attachments by drag-and-drop and
      paste, not only through the file picker. Michael, via shared
      tasklist TSK-020: "On the html dashboard, the user can also drag
      and drog attachment to any existing task... They can drag the
      file(s) to the task card in order to attach. Also the user can
      paste if that is a file or picture, also convert that to
      attachment." Each tasklist card highlights while a file is
      dragged over it and accepts a drop or a paste (when the card has
