4.02  2026-08-25

    - TKT-525. A backward move that resets an already-done required item
      now says why, on the card. Reported by zen-framework as "moving a
      card into Backlog resets ALL prior required-items to pending,
      keeping their proof" - reproduced and root-caused: Backlog is
      always the structurally-first column, so a move into it is always
      the most extreme case of TKT-455's existing, intended backward-move
      design (a backward move resets every done item between destination
      and origin, deliberately, so redoing work means every check is
      satisfied again). Michael's answer: keep the reset, explain it.
      _apply_column_required_actions's backward branch now adds one
      comment per move (not one per item) naming the origin and
      destination columns, listing which required item(s) reset, and
      reassuring the reader that their proof was left untouched - only
      when something actually reset; a backward move that resets nothing
      adds no comment.

4.01  2026-08-25

    - TKT-523. Task List section: a card's own text can now be edited in
      place - click it, type, Enter/blur saves, Escape discards. The
      section also auto-refreshes every second, matching the ticket
      board's own cadence, without a refresh tick ever clobbering an
      in-progress edit. `tira.tasklist.update` now accepts `--text` (it
      previously only accepted `--status`); status-only and text-only
      updates each leave the other field untouched.
      Found and fixed a real bug while building the refresh-safe part:
      the section's render used `replaceChildren`, which detaches and
      reattaches every card on every refresh even when nothing about that
      card actually changed - including the card currently being edited,
      whose focused input lost focus (and therefore the edit) on the very
      next tick. Caught live by the browser test. Fixed by replacing the
      blind rebuild with a positional reconciliation that only moves a
      node when its position genuinely differs from where it already is.

