3.53  2026-08-23

    - TKT-361. The 600s rule.suspend ceiling was shorter than either
      gate this repo runs - coverage at 846s, pre-push at 15m and
      counting - so the commonest legitimate reason for a suspension,
      waiting on a gate, always outlasted the longest suspension that
      could be given. The same reason was re-supplied over and over as
      it kept expiring mid-gate.

    - Fixed: tira.rule.suspend accepts an optional --pid. A
      pid-scoped suspension lifts the moment that process is gone,
