2.90  2026-08-19

    - TKT-422. agent-still sent an identical Telegram message on every
      police poll that found the agent still stopped, roughly once a
      minute for as long as the stall lasted - confirmed live by a
      screenshot of the same message landing on the owner's phone,
      seconds apart, only the elapsed-time figure changing. Every other
      bridge-routed rule is throttled by the bridge's own seen/settle
      tracking; agent-still goes straight to Telegram on purpose, because
      the one rule whose subject is the agent having stopped is the one
      rule the bridge cannot usefully deliver to - and going around the
      bridge meant going around the only thing that would have stopped
      it repeating.

