      and an edit made in the browser was invisible until the agent happened
      to re-read the card.

    - The signal was already recorded and nothing read it. Every route on the
      browser dashboard puts the signed-in person on the change, so the engine
      records who acted and history entries carry an author: an edit made
      there has one, an edit made from the CLI does not.

    - card-changed-by-owner compares rather than remembers - the newest change
      on a card was made by somebody who is not the agent working it - so it
      settles the moment the agent touches the card, and there is no stored
      timestamp to go stale or be quietly reset. No age, because a change is
      not more or less true an hour later.

