2.42  2026-08-17

    - TKT-281, reported by Zenandi and reproduced rather than taken on trust:
      tira.ticket.move accepted --sdlc-gate, ignored it, and exited 0 after
      printing the whole card - which reads as confirmation because the card
      is right there. A card at G2 moved with --sdlc-gate G9 came back in the
      new column, still at G2.
    - The same shape as --field in 2.24, and it costs more. Their board's
      rules require the gate to be updated with every transition, so "move
      and set the gate" is the most natural thing to type there: the correct
      action expressed in one command, silently half-done.
    - Refused now, naming the command that does set a gate, which is the
      mechanism 2.24 put in place for exactly this. The alternative - letting
      move carry the gate, one command doing the whole transition, which is
      what the reporter asked for - is recorded on the card as a decision
      rather than an oversight. The refusal wins because it cannot do the
      wrong thing quietly and it is reversible: teaching move to act on the
      flag later is an addition, un-teaching callers that it works is not.

