2.38  2026-08-17

    - TKT-278, his question: "is there any policy to remind the agent a card
      has been sitting on the same column without any changes for too long?"
      Partly, and the missing half was the important one. card-duration
      measures how long a card has been in one NAMED column and says nothing
      about whether anybody is working it; checklist-idle watches the
      checklist alone; board-still asks the right question - has anything
      happened - of a whole board, and there was no per-card version. So a
      card moved into verify twenty minutes ago and abandoned was
      indistinguishable from one moved in twenty minutes ago and being
      verified right now.
    - card-still reports a card nothing has happened to for longer than an
      age, in any column work happens in, reading the same last_updated stamp
      board-still reads for a board - every kind of activity touches it. No
      column to name, so one policy covers what previously took five.
    - Columns work does not happen in are left alone. A card resting in the
      backlog has not started and a card in an ending is over, and reporting
      those would put every board permanently in violation of its own
      history.
    - Proved by measuring dwell instead: with the rule reading when the card
      arrived in its column rather than when anything last happened to it, a
      card being worked that minute is reported - which is the noise this
      exists to avoid, and the difference the question turned on.
    - And each column says how long is too long, which was his refinement:
      "there is a protection-card option to set for it... how long it can
      stay in backlog; or some columns called done, or released ones - those
      don't need setting, so there won't be spamming messages." Every column
      has carried its own limit in minutes and its own watched flag since
      they were added; tira.stale has judged cards by them all along and no
      rule ever had. card-still asks the column first, falls back to the age
      the policy was declared with, and leaves an unwatched column alone
      however old its cards are.

2.37  2026-08-16

    - TKT-276, his request: an upgrade is traced until it is finished rather
      than announced and forgotten. The upgrade notice asked the agent to do
