    - rules-undeclared reports a rule this board has neither declared nor
      declined, with a reference and the same escalation every other rule
      has, and settles only when every rule has an answer. Declining counts:
      the point is that nothing is left unconsidered.
    - It traces the part that can be observed and claims nothing else.
      Whether the changes were read cannot be checked, and a rule that
      settles on a promise is worse than no rule - so what is watched is the
      gap the reading is for, which tira.policy.undeclared already answers.
    - Answering some of them leaves it open, which is the whole of the
      question he asked.
    - TKT-277, also his: a settlement is not an ending, and the line has to
      say so. "Most agents think the last settle statement as end and all
      done and forget everything." A settlement is written in the shape of a
      violation and arrives last, so it reads as a closing statement - and
      this board had 84 violations outstanding while settlements were
      landing on the same channel. Every pass that writes anything now ends
      with how many are still open and which, and a pass with nothing to say
      still writes nothing, because silence has to go on meaning silence.
    - The tail obeys the action, which the suite caught at once: without that
      filter a board whose rules are all log-only - a policy being tuned,
      deliberately out of the way - started getting bridge lines about them,
      breaking the promise that only what a policy asked for reaches the
      agent.
    - Three catalogue guards caught the new rule, which is what they are for:
      the guide must show it, two tests keep their own list of every rule,
      and one asserts every declared rule fires against a board built to
      break them all. That last one cannot hold for this rule - its subject
      is a rule left unanswered, and that board answers every rule - so it is
      exempt there by name and with the reason, and the exemption itself is
      asserted so it cannot grow unnoticed.

