2.14  2026-08-16

    - TKT-237: what is still outstanding can be asked for.
      tira.police.outstanding answers with one entry per finding rather
      than one per telling, carrying the rule, the card, how many times it
      has been said, when it started and how loud it has become. A finding
      that was dealt with leaves the list, which is the half that makes it
      worth reading.
    - The bridge is a stream and is right to be one, but a stream can only
      be read from where you joined it: it replays everything on connect
      and repeats each finding as it climbs. The enforcement log is flat -
      every row is something that happened, and nothing on a row says
      whether it is still true. So the question could not be asked, and
      therefore was not.
    - Measured on this project's own board before it existed: one finding
      open two and a half hours, escalating note to critical, read four
      times and acted on never, and the outstanding set looked at for the
      first time only because the owner asked why. An answer that depends
      on somebody remembering to look is what this subsystem exists to
      remove.
    - Proved by making it answer with the closed findings as well, which is
      what the log already does: the assertion that a dealt-with finding
      leaves the list fails, and nothing else does.
    - TKT-250: one way to say which board, not three. The owner's
      instruction: no command takes --project any more, TIRA_HOME is the
      only selector, it holds a name the machine resolves, and every
      command resolves it internally.
    - There were three ways - a flag, the environment, and discovery from
      the working directory - and three ways to say one thing is three
      behaviours to keep in agreement. They had already stopped agreeing:
      the dashboard replaces the environment value from the working
      directory, so a value passed in was discarded rather than preferred.
    - 254 uses across 97 test files moved to naming the board the way real
      usage names it, which is the fault TKT-229 fixed for the browser gate
      and left everywhere else. The tools moved with them.
    - Two things name a folder rather than select a board and say so:
      creating one, and importing one, which now takes --dir like creation
      does. A board that does not exist yet cannot be resolved from a name.
    - The restart carries the board in the environment instead of on the
      command line, set rather than inherited, which is the guarantee the
      flag used to give.
    - It uncovered a defect rather than causing one: reading TIRA_HOME
      emptied it, because Encode::decode consumes its source without
      LEAVE_SRC. Harmless while a flag could carry the board, and fatal the
      moment the environment is the only way - the first command in a
      process took the value and every command after it saw an empty
      string.

