    - A floor under the suite, so the two files that reach a board through
      a resolver cannot quietly become none again.
    - TKT-232: the messages the code prints are a surface too. The board's
      location is kept from the agent working a project, and that is
      enforced on SKILLS.md, on three help surfaces and on the question
      reference - every one of them a document. Nothing read the modules,
      and it had already drifted there: three messages named the selector,
      two of them added last release in guards whose own comment says they
      say nothing about what they were given. They did not quote the
      value. They named the flag, which tells a reader that a flag
      pointing at a board exists at all.
    - Reworded, and a guard added that reads every module and asks the same
      question of anything it prints. Comments are exempt: a comment has
      to be able to explain why the rule exists, and nobody is handed a
      comment. The guard also holds the refusals to still saying
      something, because a message emptied of content would pass a check
      for what it must not contain and help nobody - proved by emptying
      them and watching it fail.
