      that allows one and asked whether the limit was broken. It was not -
      police raised it and kept raising it - but its reminders go to the
      bridge and nothing was reading the bridge. Police found that too,
      and reported it down the bridge.
    - Its other route is the owner's terminal, which opens on the pass
      where a violation has been seen five times. That wait is deliberate
      and right for every rule with a working channel in the meantime, and
      wrong for the one rule whose channel is the thing being reported.
      Measured on this project's own board: four tellings over sixty-four
      minutes, at urgent, delivered to neither party.
    - So this rule escalates on its first telling, through a per-rule
      threshold rather than a special case at the delivery site - the
      delivery was never the fault. Every other rule keeps the wait it
      had, and a test holds that: the obvious louder fix, escalating
