      time. _backup_home names its directory from the absolute path of the
      board "so two projects on one machine never write over each other",
      and returns undef rather than inventing a fallback when it has
      nothing to name. The store now does both: the discovered board, and
      a refusal when there is no board to name. Every caller has one -
      police discovers a board before it can watch anything - so nothing
      has to be made up, and inventing a name is what made the sharing
      silent.
    - This is the second half of the report that produced 2.04, and the
      half that did not reproduce by hand: passing --project always
      produces a correct per-board store, so the fault is invisible to
      anyone who tests that way.
    - Nothing is migrated. A machine that has been policing boards from
      their own directories has a .tira-police/here holding whichever
      boards passed through it, and after this nothing reads or writes it
      again - each board starts a store of its own. That means the first
      run after upgrading announces the version to every board that had
      been sharing, which is right: they were never told the first time.

