      the words written for it, and nobody was listening. The owner found
      it before the agent did.
    - Nothing recorded that the bridge had been read, so "nobody is
      listening" was not a fact anybody could observe. Reading it now
      leaves a mark, made by the reading rather than by a claim about it:
      asking for the backlog is what tailing the bridge does, and there
      is deliberately no command to acknowledge it and no flag to set.
    - A tail left running keeps the mark fresh on every poll, so an agent
      doing the right thing is never reported for it - asserted by
      running the real follow loop with its waiting stubbed out and the
      clock moving on between rounds.
    - A bridge with nothing on it is not unread. There is nothing to
      read, and sending an agent to look at an empty file is how it
      learns to stop looking.
    - The period is required. How long an agent may go without looking is
      a decision about how it works: a minute is absurd on a board polled
      hourly and a day useless on one being worked now.

