      had shipped days before.
    - Nine wrong notes in a single pass is not merely annoying: the
      policies guide's own warning is that a channel which buzzes
      constantly is one nobody reads, so a rule wrong nine times
      immediately costs the bridge its standing rather than the rule its
      credibility.
    - tira.column.update --terminal marks a column as an ending and the
      rule asks the board. Still asks the board rather than taking a
      column on the policy: that reasoning was right when the rule
