1.69  2026-08-14
    - TKT-153: a replayed backlog is introduced as a replay. The bridge
      prints what is outstanding when it starts and then live traffic,
      with nothing between them, so a pile of old lines about cards that
      have since moved reads as a storm of new violations. One line now
      says how many are outstanding and the span they were raised over.
    - zen-framework asked for it and offered their own false report as
      the evidence: they read exactly such a pile as one rule firing
      across every discarded card, and filed TKT-136 on it. It is the
      other half of 1.51's settlement lines rather than a substitute - a
      settlement says a violation stopped being true, and does not say
      that the twelve lines in front of you are history.
    - Their second choice, marking every replayed line, was not taken: an
      agent parses these, and changing the shape of all of them for a
      distinction that only matters at the boundary costs more than it
