      message telling somebody where an option belongs is a document, and
      it no longer belongs anywhere.
    - Sessions still have tokens and a token still ends its own session,
      which is where a token is really used. The browser flow passes its
      token in the request body and never through this parser.

1.58  2026-08-14
    - TKT-133: the work log says who changed the card. Every record write
      journals the change and stamps it with the author the engine
      happens to be holding, and only four methods ever set one - so a
      checklist item, a gate, a piece of evidence and an assignment were
      all recorded as written by nobody.
    - Worse than an oversight: gate.add and evidence.add took an author,
      stored it inside the entry, and did not use it for the log. The
      name was collected and then not used for the one thing the log
      exists to answer.
    - Reported from developer-dashboard, where a reminder collector
      resumed the session an agent was working in every fifteen minutes.
      A headless copy read that a card was in Todo and moved it to
