0.53  2026-08-07
    - Per-field history (DD-443): every record write is journaled field
      by field to .tira/history/<REF>.jsonl, whichever command performed
      it, with before and after values, the change time, the operation,
      and an optional validated author. Creation seeds birth entries,
      moves journal their column change, structural fields record that
      they changed without inlining their value, and rolled-back
      operations record nothing. tira.history.list reads it with the
      established window, since, where, count, and truncation
      semantics. History lives outside the boards, so records, content
      hashes, and board reads are untouched.

0.52  2026-08-07
    - Reads are up to 170x faster on mature boards: Cpanel::JSON::XS is
      used when installed, with core JSON::PP as the fallback. Measured
      on 138 records averaging 32KB — dashboard with titles 2076ms to
      12ms, full export 2070ms to 19ms, field-scoped search 2234ms to
      17ms. Output is byte-identical, so stored records never rewrite
      and content hashes never drift; the non-reference tolerance of
      the previous backend is preserved explicitly on every
      value-bearing path.

0.51  2026-08-07
    - Column-width toggle in every board header (owner photo, message
      2976): Standard keeps today's fixed-width scrollable columns, Fit
      all shrinks every column so a wide board — the reported case had
      twelve — is fully visible without sideways scrolling. The choice
      applies to all boards, persists in browser storage, degrades to
      Standard when storage is blocked, and narrow screens keep
      scrollable columns while the desktop preference is preserved.

0.50  2026-08-07
    - The dashboard's default live-refresh interval is now 60 seconds
      (was 5). `?refresh=N` still selects any positive interval and
      invalid values fall back to the new default. With 0.49's
      repaint-only-on-change cycle the board still updates in place;
      it now costs one comparison per minute instead of one every five
      seconds.

0.49  2026-08-07
    - Dialog live refresh repaints only on real change (owner video,
      message 2969): the cycle fetches the record, compares it against
      the rendered snapshot, and does nothing when identical — no
      rebuild, no linked-row refetches, no flicker. The editing guard
      now re-checks after the fetch returns, so a refresh response
      already in flight when an editor opens can never evict it.

